@node Project Overview, Technology Stack, Introduction, Introduction
@section Project Overview

Tootsville is a 3D virtual world game built with modern web technologies. The client is implemented using React and Three.js, providing a rich, interactive experience across multiple platforms.

@subsection Key Features

@itemize
@item Real-time 3D graphics with Three.js
@item Cross-platform support (desktop, mobile, smart TV)
@item WebSocket-based communication with Lisp server
@item Modern React architecture with hooks
@item Comprehensive unit testing
@item Accessibility-first design
@end itemize

@node Technology Stack, Design Principles, Project Overview, Introduction
@section Technology Stack

@subsection Frontend Technologies

@table @asis
@item React 18.2.0
Modern UI library with hooks and functional components

@item Three.js 0.157.0
3D graphics library for WebGL rendering

@item React Three Fiber 8.15.0
React renderer for Three.js

@item React Three Drei 9.88.0
Useful helpers for React Three Fiber

@item Zustand 4.4.0
Lightweight state management
@end table

@subsection Development Tools

@table @asis
@item React Scripts 5.0.1
Build tool and development server

@item Jest
Unit testing framework

@item ESLint
Code linting and formatting

@item Webpack
Module bundling
@end table

@node Design Principles, , Technology Stack, Introduction
@section Design Principles

@subsection Object-Oriented Design

All components follow object-oriented principles with clear separation of concerns:

@itemize
@item Single Responsibility Principle
@item Open/Closed Principle
@item Dependency Inversion
@item Interface Segregation
@end itemize

@subsection Component Architecture

Components are designed to be:

@itemize
@item Reusable and composable
@item Testable in isolation
@item Accessible by default
@item Performance optimized
@end itemize

