@node System Overview, Component Hierarchy, Architecture, Architecture
@section System Overview

The Tootsville client follows a layered architecture:

@example
┌─────────────────────────────────────┐
│              UI Layer               │
│  (React Components + Three.js)      │
├─────────────────────────────────────┤
│           State Layer               │
│         (Zustand Stores)            │
├─────────────────────────────────────┤
│         Service Layer               │
│    (Communication, Platform)        │
├─────────────────────────────────────┤
│         External APIs               │
│    (WebSocket, WebGL, etc.)         │
└─────────────────────────────────────┘
@end example

@node Component Hierarchy, State Management, System Overview, Architecture
@section Component Hierarchy

@example
App
├── ErrorBoundary
├── GameProvider
├── GameWorld
│   ├── WorldScene
│   ├── Ground
│   ├── WorldObjects
│   ├── Character
│   ├── WorldItem
│   └── WeatherEffects
├── GameHUD
├── LoginScreen
└── LoadingScreen
@end example

@node State Management, Communication Layer, Component Hierarchy, Architecture
@section State Management

State is managed using Zustand stores:

@itemize
@item @code{GameStore} - Global game state
@item @code{UserStore} - User authentication and profile
@item @code{WorldStore} - 3D world state
@item @code{UISStore} - User interface state
@end itemize

@node Communication Layer, 3D Rendering, State Management, Architecture
